# Task Ticket Template

This rule defines the standard template for creating new task tickets (e.g., GitHub Issues) in this project. Following this template ensures consistency and provides clear instructions, especially for junior developers.

**Важное правило языка:**
*   Все плейсхолдеры в квадратных скобках (например, `[Brief, Action-Oriented Title]`, `[Specific action for the developer]`) являются **английскими** ключевыми словами, описывающими ожидаемый контент. **Не переводите их.**
*   Текст, который вы **вписываете** вместо этих плейсхолдеров при создании тикета, должен быть на **русском языке**.

## Ticket Structure (XML Definition)

Use the following conceptual XML structure to guide the creation of the final Markdown ticket. The actual ticket should be created in **Markdown format** following this structure.

```xml
<TaskTicket>
    <Title>[TaskID]: [Brief, Action-Oriented Title]</Title> <!-- e.g., [TASK-SP1-001]: Настройка Репозитория -->
    <ID>[TaskID]</ID> <!-- e.g., TASK-SP1-001 -->
    <RelatedScenario link="mdc:path/to/feature/file.md#scenario-scenarioid">[Link Text]</RelatedScenario> <!-- Example Markdown Link: [S01.01 Пересылка вакансии...](mdc:features/Reconstructed_F01_from_issues.md#scenario-s0101-пересылка-вакансии-и-получение-тикета) -->
    <RoadmapItem optional="true">[Link to MVP_Roadmap.md item]</RoadmapItem>
    <DependsOn optional="true">[Link to prerequisite issue, e.g., #123]</DependsOn>

    <Description>
        [Provide a brief (1-2 sentence) overview of the task and its goal.]
    </Description>

    <ImplementationChecklist>
        <Item>Step 1: [Specific action for the developer]</Item>
        <Item>Step 2: [Specific action for the developer]</Item>
        <Item>...</Item>
        <Item>Ensure code adheres to project linting/formatting standards ([NS05.01](mdc:features/Reconstructed_NF05_from_issues.md#scenario-ns0501-стандартизация-инструментов-разработки))</Item>
        <Item>Write/update unit tests covering the changes ([NS05.02](mdc:features/Reconstructed_NF05_from_issues.md#scenario-ns0502-организация-процесса-pull-request))</Item>
    </ImplementationChecklist>

    <AcceptanceCriteria>
        <Criterion>Criterion 1: [Measurable condition that must be met for the task to be 'Done']</Criterion>
        <Criterion>Criterion 2: [Measurable condition that must be met for the task to be 'Done']</Criterion>
        <Criterion>...</Criterion>
        <Criterion>All CI checks pass ([NS01.02](mdc:features/Reconstructed_NF01_from_issues.md#scenario-ns0102-настройка-cicd-для-автоматических-сборок))</Criterion>
    </AcceptanceCriteria>

    <Notes optional="true">
        [Any additional context, considerations, or potential gotchas.]
    </Notes>
</TaskTicket>
```

**Explanation of Fields (for generating Markdown output):**

*   **Title (`<Title>`):** Формат заголовка задачи: `[TaskID]: Краткое название задачи`. `TaskID` должен совпадать со значением в поле ID. Пример: `[TASK-SP1-001]: Настройка Репозитория bot-svc`.
*   **ID (`<ID>`):** Уникальный идентификатор задачи в формате `TASK-SP<SprintNumber>-<TaskNumber>`, например, `TASK-SP1-001`. Этот же ID используется в начале заголовка. Формат в теле тикета: `**ID:** \`TASK-SP1-001\``.
*   **Related Scenario (`<RelatedScenario>`):** Provide a direct **Markdown link** to the relevant scenario within the corresponding feature file (use the `mdc:` link format as shown in the XML comment). Format as `**Related Scenario:** [Link Text](mdc:path...)`.
*   **Checklist (`<ImplementationChecklist>`):** Break down the task into small, concrete steps a junior developer can follow. Use Markdown list format (`* [ ] Step...`). Include standard checks like linting and testing.
*   **Acceptance Criteria (`<AcceptanceCriteria>`):** Define specific, verifiable conditions that prove the task is completed correctly. Use Markdown list format (`* [ ] Criterion...`). Reference CI checks.
*   Other fields map directly to Markdown headings like `**Roadmap Item:**`, `**Depends On:**`, `**Description:**`, `**Notes:**`.

**REMEMBER:** The final output (e.g., in a GitHub Issue) should be **Markdown**, using this XML structure as a guide.
